module

public import LeanCategories.ForMathlib.DoubleCosetOrbit
public import LeanCategories.ForMathlib.SchreierStabilizer
public import LeanCategories.Lattices.Valued.CuspDescent
public import LeanCategories.Lattices.Valued.CobleCusps

/-!
# The plane stabilizer's line orbits, and the discriminant image from Schreier data

Two consequences of the general orbit/double-coset dictionary
(`LeanCategories.ForMathlib.DoubleCosetOrbit`) and of Schreier's generators for a point stabilizer
(`LeanCategories.ForMathlib.SchreierStabilizer`) at the integral orthogonal group `O(L)`:

* **The integral plane stabilizer's orbits on primitive lines are double cosets.** For a primitive
  isotropic plane `P` and a primitive isotropic line `V` of `L`, the orbits of
  `Stab_{O(L)}(P)` on the `O(L)`-translates of `V` are the double cosets
  `Stab_{O(L)}(P) \ O(L) / Stab_{O(L)}(V)` (`planeStabilizerOrbitsEquivDoubleCoset`). This is the
  flag-incidence operation of the descent page: the plane is held fixed and the lines in play are
  the translates of one line, so the plane stabilizer plays the role of `Γ` and no transitivity of
  `O(L)` on the lines of `P` is asserted.
* **That double-coset space is finite when the acting group has finite index.** For
  `Γ : FiniteIndexSubgroup L` and a primitive isotropic line `V`, the double cosets
  `Γ \ O(L) / Stab_{O(L)}(V)` are finite, with at most `[O(L) : Γ]` of them
  (`finite_quotient_lineStabilizer`, `natCard_quotient_lineStabilizer_le_index`). This is the
  finiteness of the line count in a descent fibre, and it is the finite-index hypothesis, not a
  computation at a finite quotient, that supplies it.
* **The discriminant image of an integral stabilizer is generated by the discriminant actions of the
  Schreier loops** (`discriminantRangeImage_eq_closure_schreier`): if a subgroup `H ≤ O(L)` is the
  point stabilizer of an `O(L)`-set `Σ` at `b`, and `S` generates `O(L)` with transversal `t` of the
  orbit of `b`, then `ρ_L(H)` is generated by the `ρ_L ((t (s • q))⁻¹ * s * t q)`. The equality is
  derived from Schreier's theorem and `MonoidHom.map_closure`, not assumed.

## The input action of the last theorem

The set `Ω` is the orbit of the residue submodule `L̄_m = L / mM` in `M / mM`, and the action of
`O(L)` on it must be the action through the *module* action `π_m : O(L) → Aut_ℤ(M / mM)`. The
permutation action on the set of submodules has a strictly larger kernel (`κ_m ⊇ K̄_m`, the
discriminant page's `lem:orbit-permutation-not-module-action`), so a stabilizer computed inside the
permutation image is not the integral stabilizer and its image under `ρ_L` is not the discriminant
image. The hypothesis `hH : H = MulAction.stabilizer (OrthogonalGroup L) b` is where a caller
discharges this: `lem:congruence-stabilizer-preimage` identifies the stabilizer of the residue
submodule in the module action with `Stab_{O(L)}(L)`, and by `cor:stabilizer-modulus` the
congruence kernel at a modulus with `mM ⊆ e₂L` lies in `ker ρ_L`.

## Search record (LC-09)

`scripts/formalization_corpus.py search` at the manifest head `6d97e8ad` under
`primitive isotropic lines stabilizer orbits` (no files), `discriminant representation orthogonal
group stabilizer image` (TauCeti roadmap `Completed/OrthogonalSpinGroups/Suggested.lean`), and
`discriminant of a translate of a lattice isometry` / `dual lattice of an isometric image
discriminant form` (TauCeti `Algebra/Module/ZLattice/Shell.lean`, `.../RealModel.lean`). No source
has the transport of the next section; the nearest owners model a lattice with its dual
(`ZLattice`), not this repository's `IntegralLatticeCat` with its separate discriminant module.

## Not formalized here

The page's item 3 factorizes each `ρ_L (k_{s,p})` through the discriminant isometries
`α_s(L_p) : A_{L_p} → A_{sL_p}` between the translates of `L` in the orbit
(`thm:discriminant-transport-functor`). That transport is not available in this development: an
`IntegralLatticeCat` object carries its own discriminant module, and there is no owner of `A_{tL}`
together with the comparison `A_L ≃ A_{tL}` for a translate `tL` of `L` by an isometry. The
generated-subgroup equality below is stated with the discriminant actions at the single lattice `L`,
which is what `ρ_L` is defined on; the factorized form would refine the *same* equality and is left
open rather than approximated.
-/

@[expose] public section

open MulAction

namespace LeanCategories.Lattices.Valued

universe u

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R] {L : IntegralLatticeCat R}

/-! ## The plane stabilizer's orbits on primitive lines -/

/-- **The integral plane stabilizer's orbits on primitive lines are double cosets.** For a primitive
isotropic plane `P` and a primitive isotropic line `V` of `L`, the orbits of `Stab_{O(L)}(P)` on the
`O(L)`-translates of `V` are the double cosets of `Stab_{O(L)}(P)` and `Stab_{O(L)}(V)`.

The codomain restricts the quotient to the orbits that meet the `O(L)`-orbit of `V`: the plane
stabilizer's orbits on the lines that are `O(L)`-translates of `V`, which is the fibre a flag
computation visits. -/
noncomputable def planeStabilizerOrbitsEquivDoubleCoset [IsDomain R]
    (P : PrimitiveIsotropic L 2) (V : PrimitiveIsotropic L 1) :
    DoubleCoset.Quotient (MulAction.stabilizer (OrthogonalGroup L) P : Set (OrthogonalGroup L))
        (MulAction.stabilizer (OrthogonalGroup L) V : Set (OrthogonalGroup L)) ≃
      {o : orbitRel.Quotient (MulAction.stabilizer (OrthogonalGroup L) P)
          (PrimitiveIsotropic L 1) //
        ∃ q, q ∈ MulAction.orbit (OrthogonalGroup L) V ∧ Quotient.mk'' q = o} :=
  DoubleCoset.orbitRelQuotientEquivDoubleCoset _ V

/-! ## Finiteness from the finite index -/

/-- **The line double cosets of a finite-index subgroup are finite.** -/
theorem finite_quotient_lineStabilizer [IsDomain R] (Γ : FiniteIndexSubgroup L)
    (V : PrimitiveIsotropic L 1) :
    Finite (DoubleCoset.Quotient (Γ.toSubgroup : Set (OrthogonalGroup L))
      (MulAction.stabilizer (OrthogonalGroup L) V : Set (OrthogonalGroup L))) := by
  have := Γ.finiteIndex
  exact DoubleCoset.finite_quotient_of_finiteIndex _ Γ.toSubgroup

/-- **A finite-index subgroup has at most its index of line double cosets.** -/
theorem natCard_quotient_lineStabilizer_le_index [IsDomain R] (Γ : FiniteIndexSubgroup L)
    (V : PrimitiveIsotropic L 1) :
    Nat.card (DoubleCoset.Quotient (Γ.toSubgroup : Set (OrthogonalGroup L))
      (MulAction.stabilizer (OrthogonalGroup L) V : Set (OrthogonalGroup L))) ≤
      Γ.toSubgroup.index := by
  have := Γ.finiteIndex
  exact DoubleCoset.natCard_quotient_le_index _ Γ.toSubgroup

/-! ## The discriminant image from Schreier data -/

/-- **The discriminant image of a point stabilizer is generated by the Schreier loops.** If `S`
generates `O(L)`, `t` is a transversal of the orbit of the base point `b` of an `O(L)`-set `Σ`
(`t q • b = q`, `t b = 1`), and `H` is the stabilizer of `b`, then
`ρ_L(H) = ⟨ρ_L ((t (s • q))⁻¹ * s * t q)⟩` inside `O(A_L)`.

The proof is `Subgroup.closure_schreierLoops_eq_stabilizer` followed by `MonoidHom.map_closure`: the
image of a generated subgroup is generated by the images of the generators. `hH` is the caller's
obligation that `H` really is the point stabilizer of the module action (see the module docstring);
without it the statement would be about the stabilizer of whatever action was supplied. -/
theorem discriminantRangeImage_eq_closure_schreier [IsDomain R]
    (hL : IsFractionFieldPerfect R L) {Ω : Type u} [MulAction (OrthogonalGroup L) Ω] (b : Ω)
    (H : Subgroup (OrthogonalGroup L)) (hH : H = MulAction.stabilizer (OrthogonalGroup L) b)
    (S : Set (OrthogonalGroup L)) (hS : Subgroup.closure S = ⊤)
    (t : Ω → OrthogonalGroup L) (ht : ∀ q, t q • b = q) (hb : t b = 1) :
    discriminantRangeImage hL H =
      Subgroup.closure ((fun x : OrthogonalGroup L × Ω =>
        ⟨(OrthogonalGroup.discriminantRepresentation hL) ((t (x.1 • x.2))⁻¹ * x.1 * t x.2),
          ⟨_, rfl⟩⟩) '' (S ×ˢ MulAction.orbit (OrthogonalGroup L) b)) := by
  rw [hH, discriminantRangeImage_eq_map_rangeRestrict,
    ← Subgroup.closure_schreierLoops_eq_stabilizer S hS b t ht hb]
  rw [MonoidHom.map_closure]
  congr 1
  ext y
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨-, ⟨⟨s, q⟩, ⟨hs, hq⟩, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨(s, q), ⟨hs, hq⟩, rfl⟩
  · rintro ⟨⟨s, q⟩, ⟨hs, hq⟩, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨_, ⟨⟨s, q⟩, ⟨hs, hq⟩, rfl⟩, rfl⟩

/-! ## The worked plane of `T_Co` -/

/-- **The worked plane action**: for the Coble lattice `T_Co`, the exhibited primitive isotropic
plane `coblePlane` and the exhibited primitive isotropic line `cobleLine`, the orbits of the
integral plane stabilizer on the `O(T_Co)`-translates of the line are the double cosets of the plane
stabilizer and the line stabilizer. -/
noncomputable def coblePlaneStabilizerOrbitsEquivDoubleCoset :
    DoubleCoset.Quotient
        (MulAction.stabilizer (OrthogonalGroup cobleLattice) coblePlane :
          Set (OrthogonalGroup cobleLattice))
        (MulAction.stabilizer (OrthogonalGroup cobleLattice) cobleLine :
          Set (OrthogonalGroup cobleLattice)) ≃
      {o : orbitRel.Quotient (MulAction.stabilizer (OrthogonalGroup cobleLattice) coblePlane)
          (PrimitiveIsotropic cobleLattice 1) //
        ∃ q, q ∈ MulAction.orbit (OrthogonalGroup cobleLattice) cobleLine ∧
          Quotient.mk'' q = o} :=
  planeStabilizerOrbitsEquivDoubleCoset coblePlane cobleLine

/-- The worked plane action is a finite description: the line double cosets of the Coble stable
orthogonal group are finite. -/
theorem finite_cobleDoubleCoset_line :
    Finite (DoubleCoset.Quotient (cobleKernelSubgroup.toSubgroup :
      Set (OrthogonalGroup cobleLattice))
      (MulAction.stabilizer (OrthogonalGroup cobleLattice) cobleLine :
        Set (OrthogonalGroup cobleLattice))) :=
  finite_quotient_lineStabilizer cobleKernelSubgroup cobleLine

end LeanCategories.Lattices.Valued
